Subject: [PATCH upwell-2] catalog: wait up to 2 minutes for the SQLite lock

pgcopydb's COPY, index and vacuum workers all record their progress in one
SQLite catalog. A worker that finds it locked retried for 5 seconds and then
failed. On the droplet (2026-10-14) an index worker built index 17071 on the
target, could not record it within 5 s ("database is locked" on
"update summary set done_time_epoch ..."), and the whole base copy of a
300 GB database failed. The three retry loops (BEGIN, prepare, step) now wait
up to 2 minutes.

diff --git a/src/bin/pgcopydb/catalog.c b/src/bin/pgcopydb/catalog.c
index 4fac961..8d6e810 100644
--- a/src/bin/pgcopydb/catalog.c
+++ b/src/bin/pgcopydb/catalog.c
@@ -1968,7 +1968,13 @@ catalog_begin(DatabaseCatalog *catalog, bool immediate)
 	{
 		ConnectionRetryPolicy retryPolicy = { 0 };
 
-		int maxT = 5;            /* 5s */
+		/*
+		 * Upwell patch (upwell-2): 5 s was too short.  Every COPY, index and
+		 * vacuum worker writes its progress here; on a busy work volume a
+		 * writer can hold the lock longer, and giving up failed a whole base
+		 * copy whose index had been built ("database is locked").
+		 */
+		int maxT = 120;          /* 2 min */
 		int maxSleepTime = 350;  /* 350ms */
 		int baseSleepTime = 10;  /* 10ms */
 
@@ -10878,7 +10884,13 @@ catalog_sql_prepare(sqlite3 *db, const char *sql, SQLiteQuery *query)
 	{
 		ConnectionRetryPolicy retryPolicy = { 0 };
 
-		int maxT = 5;            /* 5s */
+		/*
+		 * Upwell patch (upwell-2): 5 s was too short.  Every COPY, index and
+		 * vacuum worker writes its progress here; on a busy work volume a
+		 * writer can hold the lock longer, and giving up failed a whole base
+		 * copy whose index had been built ("database is locked").
+		 */
+		int maxT = 120;          /* 2 min */
 		int maxSleepTime = 150;  /* 150ms */
 		int baseSleepTime = 10;  /* 10ms */
 
@@ -11167,7 +11179,13 @@ catalog_sql_step(SQLiteQuery *query)
 	{
 		ConnectionRetryPolicy retryPolicy = { 0 };
 
-		int maxT = 5;            /* 5s */
+		/*
+		 * Upwell patch (upwell-2): 5 s was too short.  Every COPY, index and
+		 * vacuum worker writes its progress here; on a busy work volume a
+		 * writer can hold the lock longer, and giving up failed a whole base
+		 * copy whose index had been built ("database is locked").
+		 */
+		int maxT = 120;          /* 2 min */
 		int maxSleepTime = 350;  /* 350ms */
 		int baseSleepTime = 10;  /* 10ms */
 
